---
// src/pages/test2.astro - Typography Comparison Lab for Book Titles & Body Font Pairings
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="UTF-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
	<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
	<title>Typography Comparison Lab - Decoding The Burn</title>

	<!-- Google Fonts for all requested pairings including Inter, Public Sans, and Work Sans -->
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
	<link
		href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@600;700;800;900&family=Fira+Sans:ital,wght@0,600;0,700;0,800;1,600&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&family=Literata:ital,opsz,wght@0,7..72,400;0,7..72,600;1,7..72,400&family=Merriweather:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Montserrat:wght@700;800;900&family=PT+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400&family=Public+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;0,800;1,400&family=Source+Sans+3:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;0,800;0,900;1,400;1,600&family=Work+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;0,800;1,400&display=swap"
		rel="stylesheet"
	/>

	<style>
		:root {
			--bg-app: #0a0614;
			--bg-card: #ffffff;
			--accent-purple: #7c3aed;
			--accent-dark-purple: #581c87;
			--text-subtle: #64748b;
			--border-subtle: #e2e8f0;
		}

		* {
			box-sizing: border-box;
		}

		body {
			margin: 0;
			padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 5rem;
			background-color: var(--bg-app);
			color: #f8fafc;
			font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
			-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
		}

		.lab-container {
			max-width: 1460px;
			margin: 0 auto;
		}

		.lab-header {
			text-align: center;
			margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
		}

		.lab-header h1 {
			font-size: 2.5rem;
			font-weight: 800;
			color: #ffffff;
			margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
			letter-spacing: -0.025em;
		}

		.lab-header p {
			color: #c4b5fd;
			font-size: 1.05rem;
			max-width: 860px;
			margin: 0 auto;
			line-height: 1.55;
		}

		.tag-noindex {
			display: inline-block;
			background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.2);
			color: #fca5a5;
			border: 1px solid rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4);
			padding: 0.25rem 0.85rem;
			border-radius: 9999px;
			font-size: 0.75rem;
			font-weight: 700;
			letter-spacing: 0.05em;
			text-transform: uppercase;
			margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
		}

		/* Sticky Live Filter Bar */
		.toolbar {
			background: rgba(18, 12, 34, 0.85);
			backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
			border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.25);
			border-radius: 14px;
			padding: 1.15rem 1.5rem;
			margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
			display: flex;
			flex-wrap: wrap;
			align-items: center;
			justify-content: space-between;
			gap: 0.85rem;
			position: sticky;
			top: 1rem;
			z-index: 50;
			box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
		}

		.toolbar-title {
			font-weight: 700;
			color: #ffffff;
			font-size: 0.92rem;
			letter-spacing: 0.02em;
		}

		.toolbar-buttons {
			display: flex;
			flex-wrap: wrap;
			gap: 0.45rem;
		}

		.btn-filter {
			background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
			color: #e2e8f0;
			border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
			padding: 0.45rem 0.85rem;
			border-radius: 7px;
			font-size: 0.82rem;
			cursor: pointer;
			font-weight: 600;
			transition: all 0.2s ease;
		}

		.btn-filter:hover,
		.btn-filter.active {
			background: var(--accent-purple);
			color: #ffffff;
			border-color: #a855f7;
			box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(124, 58, 237, 0.4);
		}

		/* Grid for comparisons */
		.comparisons-grid {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(430px, 1fr));
			gap: 2.25rem;
		}

		.variant-card {
			background: var(--bg-card);
			color: #0f172a;
			border-radius: 14px;
			padding: 2.25rem 2.15rem;
			box-shadow: 0 25px 50px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
			position: relative;
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
			border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
		}

		.variant-badge-bar {
			display: flex;
			justify-content: space-between;
			align-items: center;
			margin-bottom: 1.35rem;
			padding-bottom: 0.85rem;
			border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border-subtle);
		}

		.variant-pill {
			background: #f1f5f9;
			color: #334155;
			padding: 0.35rem 0.85rem;
			border-radius: 6px;
			font-size: 0.8rem;
			font-weight: 700;
		}

		.variant-pill.highlight {
			background: #f3e8ff;
			color: #6b21a8;
			border: 1px solid #d8b4fe;
		}

		.spec-pills {
			font-size: 0.82rem;
			color: #64748b;
			font-weight: 600;
		}

		.sample-book-sheet {
			flex-grow: 1;
		}

		.book-running-head {
			font-size: 0.72rem;
			font-weight: 700;
			letter-spacing: 0.06em;
			color: #94a3b8;
			text-transform: uppercase;
			padding-bottom: 0.65rem;
			margin-bottom: 1.35rem;
			border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
			display: flex;
			justify-content: space-between;
		}

		.sample-book-sheet h3 {
			margin-top: 0;
			margin-bottom: 1.15rem;
			color: var(--accent-dark-purple);
			letter-spacing: -0.015em;
			line-height: 1.25;
			border-bottom: 1.5px solid transparent;
			border-image: linear-gradient(90deg, #a855f7 0%, #c084fc 35%, transparent 75%) 1;
			padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
			text-align: left;
		}

		/* Strict: Natural left-aligned text, NOT fully justified */
		.sample-book-sheet p {
			margin: 0 0 1.05rem 0;
			text-align: left;
			text-wrap: pretty;
		}

		.sample-book-sheet p:last-child {
			margin-bottom: 0;
		}

		.sample-book-sheet strong {
			font-weight: 700;
			color: #0f172a;
		}

		.sample-book-sheet em {
			font-style: italic;
		}

		/* Dedicated Chemistry & Physics Formula Displays */
		.formula-box {
			background: #f8fafc;
			border-left: 3px solid #7c3aed;
			padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
			margin: 1.15rem 0;
			border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
			font-size: 0.88em;
			line-height: 1.45;
			color: #1e1b4b;
		}

		.formula-label {
			display: block;
			font-size: 0.72rem;
			text-transform: uppercase;
			font-weight: 700;
			letter-spacing: 0.05em;
			color: #6b21a8;
			margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
		}

		.formula-math {
			font-family: inherit;
			font-weight: 600;
			color: #0f172a;
			display: block;
			font-feature-settings: 'tnum' on, 'lnum' on;
		}

		.sci-tag {
			display: inline-block;
			background: #f1f5f9;
			border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
			padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
			border-radius: 4px;
			font-size: 0.88em;
			font-weight: 600;
			color: #334155;
			white-space: nowrap;
		}

		.chem-val {
			white-space: nowrap;
			font-feature-settings: 'tnum' on;
		}

		.font-notes {
			margin-top: 1.6rem;
			padding: 0.95rem 1.15rem;
			border-top: 1px solid #f1f5f9;
			font-size: 0.82rem;
			line-height: 1.5;
			color: #475569;
			background: #faf5ff;
			border-radius: 8px;
		}

		.font-notes strong {
			color: #581c87;
		}

		/* ==============================================================
		   1. COMBINATION 1: ARCHIVO (Bold) + SOURCE SANS 3 (Top Pick)
		   ============================================================== */
		.var-1 h3 {
			font-family: 'Archivo', sans-serif;
			font-size: 1.32rem;
			font-weight: 700;
		}
		.var-1 p, .var-1 .formula-box {
			font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif;
			font-size: 10.5pt;
			line-height: 15pt;
			color: #1e293b;
		}

		/* ==============================================================
		   2. COMBINATION 2: FIRA SANS (Bold) + PT SANS
		   ============================================================== */
		.var-2 h3 {
			font-family: 'Fira Sans', sans-serif;
			font-size: 1.28rem;
			font-weight: 700;
		}
		.var-2 p, .var-2 .formula-box {
			font-family: 'PT Sans', sans-serif;
			font-size: 10.5pt;
			line-height: 15pt;
			color: #1e293b;
		}

		/* ==============================================================
		   3. COMBINATION 3A: SOURCE SANS 3 (Bold) + LITERATA
		   ============================================================== */
		.var-3a h3 {
			font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif;
			font-size: 1.3rem;
			font-weight: 800;
		}
		.var-3a p, .var-3a .formula-box {
			font-family: 'Literata', Georgia, serif;
			font-size: 10pt;
			line-height: 14.8pt;
			color: #1e293b;
		}

		/* ==============================================================
		   4. COMBINATION 4: INTER (Precision Clinical Metric Standard)
		   Title/H3: Inter (Bold 700)
		   Body: Inter (Regular 10.25pt / 15pt)
		   ============================================================== */
		.var-inter h3 {
			font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
			font-size: 1.28rem;
			font-weight: 700;
			letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		}
		.var-inter p, .var-inter .formula-box {
			font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
			font-size: 10.25pt;
			line-height: 15pt;
			color: #1e293b;
			font-feature-settings: 'cv05' on, 'cv08' on, 'tnum' on; /* disambiguated 1, stable numerals */
		}

		/* ==============================================================
		   5. COMBINATION 5: PUBLIC SANS (Clean U.S. Federal Web Standard)
		   Title/H3: Public Sans (Bold 800)
		   Body: Public Sans (Regular 10.25pt / 15pt)
		   ============================================================== */
		.var-public h3 {
			font-family: 'Public Sans', sans-serif;
			font-size: 1.28rem;
			font-weight: 800;
			letter-spacing: -0.015em;
		}
		.var-public p, .var-public .formula-box {
			font-family: 'Public Sans', sans-serif;
			font-size: 10.25pt;
			line-height: 15pt;
			color: #1e293b;
		}

		/* ==============================================================
		   6. COMBINATION 6: WORK SANS (Architectural & Crisp Early Sans)
		   Title/H3: Work Sans (Bold 700)
		   Body: Work Sans (Regular 10.25pt / 15pt)
		   ============================================================== */
		.var-worksans h3 {
			font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
			font-size: 1.3rem;
			font-weight: 700;
			letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		}
		.var-worksans p, .var-worksans .formula-box {
			font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
			font-size: 10.25pt;
			line-height: 15pt;
			color: #1e293b;
		}

		/* ==============================================================
		   7. HYBRID: WORK SANS (Title) + SOURCE SANS 3 (Body)
		   ============================================================== */
		.var-work-source h3 {
			font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
			font-size: 1.3rem;
			font-weight: 700;
			letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		}
		.var-work-source p, .var-work-source .formula-box {
			font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif;
			font-size: 10.5pt;
			line-height: 15pt;
			color: #1e293b;
		}

		/* ==============================================================
		   8. CURRENT BOOK BASELINE (Montserrat H3 + Plus Jakarta Sans)
		   ============================================================== */
		.var-current h3 {
			font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif;
			font-size: 1.25rem;
			font-weight: 800;
		}
		.var-current p, .var-current .formula-box {
			font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif;
			font-size: 10.5pt;
			line-height: 15.5pt;
			color: #0f172a;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="lab-container">
		<header class="lab-header">
			<span class="tag-noindex">Hidden Test Lab &bull; Noindex</span>
			<h1>Book Typography Pairing Laboratory (/test2)</h1>
			<p>
				Direct side-by-side comparison of Chapter 10 with natural left-aligned body text (no forced justification) containing complex organic molecules, biophysical electrophysiology, chemical subscripts, and mathematical physics formulas.
			</p>
		</header>

		<!-- Interactive Filter Toolbar -->
		<div class="toolbar">
			<span class="toolbar-title">Filter Candidates:</span>
			<div class="toolbar-buttons">
				<button type="button" class="btn-filter active" onclick="showAll()">Show All (8 Variations)</button>
				<button type="button" class="btn-filter" onclick="filterCard('card-var-1')">1. Archivo + Source Sans 3</button>
				<button type="button" class="btn-filter" onclick="filterCard('card-var-inter')">2. Inter (Full Suite)</button>
				<button type="button" class="btn-filter" onclick="filterCard('card-var-public')">3. Public Sans</button>
				<button type="button" class="btn-filter" onclick="filterCard('card-var-worksans')">4. Work Sans</button>
				<button type="button" class="btn-filter" onclick="filterCard('card-var-work-source')">5. Work Sans + Source Sans 3</button>
				<button type="button" class="btn-filter" onclick="filterCard('card-var-2')">6. Fira Sans + PT Sans</button>
				<button type="button" class="btn-filter" onclick="filterCard('card-var-3a')">7. Source Sans 3 + Literata</button>
				<button type="button" class="btn-filter" onclick="filterCard('card-var-current')">8. Current Baseline (Montserrat)</button>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="comparisons-grid">

			<!-- 1. COMBINATION 1: ARCHIVO + SOURCE SANS 3 -->
			<div class="variant-card var-1" id="card-var-1">
				<div class="variant-badge-bar">
					<span class="variant-pill highlight">Top Pick: Technical Precision</span>
					<span class="spec-pills">Archivo (Bold 700) &bull; Source Sans 3 (10.5pt)</span>
				</div>

				<div class="sample-book-sheet">
					<div class="book-running-head">
						<span>Part III &bull; Chapter 10: Biophysical Pain Mechanisms</span>
						<span>Page 68</span>
					</div>

					<h3>The 2024 Cryo-EM Proof: Bypassing Venom to Test Real Human Receptors</h3>

					<p>
						In the landmark 2024 Cahill cryo-EM investigation at 2.7 to 3.2 Ångström resolution, researchers reconstituted full-length <strong>human ASIC1a protein</strong> into synthetic lipid nanodiscs. Stepping pH from neutral <span class="chem-val">7.40 &plusmn; 0.05</span> down to acidic <span class="chem-val">6.50</span> and <span class="chem-val">5.50</span> demonstrated that free hydronium ions (<span class="sci-tag">H<sub>3</sub>O<sup>+</sup></span>) neutralize carboxylates <span class="chem-val">Asp238</span>, <span class="chem-val">Glu239</span>, and <span class="chem-val">Asp350</span>, snapping salt bridges and opening lower transmembrane gates <span class="chem-val">Thr449 / Ser446</span>.
					</p>

					<!-- Physics & Chemistry Equation Block -->
					<div class="formula-box">
						<span class="formula-label">Biophysical Electrophysiology: Nernst &amp; Goldman Reversal Potential</span>
						<span class="formula-math">
							E<sub>rev</sub> = &minus;61.5 mV &bull; log<sub>10</sub> &times; [ (P<sub>Na</sub>[Na<sup>+</sup>]<sub>i</sub> + P<sub>K</sub>[K<sup>+</sup>]<sub>i</sub> + P<sub>Cl</sub>[Cl<sup>&minus;</sup>]<sub>o</sub>) &divide; (P<sub>Na</sub>[Na<sup>+</sup>]<sub>o</sub> + P<sub>K</sub>[K<sup>+</sup>]<sub>o</sub> + P<sub>Cl</sub>[Cl<sup>&minus;</sup>]<sub>i</sub>) ]
						</span>
						<span style="font-size: 0.82em; color: #64748b; margin-top: 0.3rem; display: block;">
							Depolarization shift: &Delta;V<sub>m</sub> = &minus;70 mV &rarr; &minus;45 mV at inward current density J<sub>Na</sub> = 14.8 &plusmn; 1.2 pA/pF.
						</span>
					</div>

					<p>
						In saliva, high-molecular-weight glycoproteins (<span class="sci-tag">MUC5B</span> and <span class="sci-tag">MUC7</span>) normally partner with bicarbonate ions (<span class="sci-tag">HCO<sub>3</sub><sup>&minus;</sup></span>) to buffer ambient oral acidity. When this buffer collapses, dental tubules leak dentinal fluid according to Hagen-Poiseuille hydrodynamics:
					</p>

					<!-- Fluid Dynamics Equation Block -->
					<div class="formula-box">
						<span class="formula-label">Hydrodynamic Fluid Shear Stress in Dentinal Microtubules</span>
						<span class="formula-math">
							Q = ( &pi; &bull; &Delta;P &bull; r<sup>4</sup> ) &divide; ( 8 &bull; &eta; &bull; L ) &nbsp;=&nbsp; 4.62 &times; 10<sup>&minus;9</sup> cm<sup>3</sup>/sec &bull; Pa
						</span>
					</div>

					<p>
						Unlike transient channels that inactivate within 100 to 300 ms, sensory nerves express <strong>ASIC3</strong> at 5&times; to 10&times; higher concentrations. Between pH 6.2 and 6.7, ASIC3 locks into an unbroken, non-inactivating window current, generating non-stop 10/10 neuropathic burning.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="font-notes">
					<strong>Why it works:</strong> Archivo gives titles industrial, nineteenth-century American grotesque stability without Montserrat's wide circular loops. Source Sans 3 renders numerals <strong>1</strong>, <strong>2024</strong>, <strong>10/10</strong>, subscripts, and superscripts with pristine Adobe clarity.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- 2. COMBINATION 4: INTER (MODERN PRECISION CLINICAL METRIC STANDARD) -->
			<div class="variant-card var-inter" id="card-var-inter">
				<div class="variant-badge-bar">
					<span class="variant-pill highlight">Inter (Digital &amp; Print Precision)</span>
					<span class="spec-pills">Inter (Bold 700) &bull; Inter (10.25pt / 15pt)</span>
				</div>

				<div class="sample-book-sheet">
					<div class="book-running-head">
						<span>Part III &bull; Chapter 10: Biophysical Pain Mechanisms</span>
						<span>Page 68</span>
					</div>

					<h3>The 2024 Cryo-EM Proof: Bypassing Venom to Test Real Human Receptors</h3>

					<p>
						In the landmark 2024 Cahill cryo-EM investigation at 2.7 to 3.2 Ångström resolution, researchers reconstituted full-length <strong>human ASIC1a protein</strong> into synthetic lipid nanodiscs. Stepping pH from neutral <span class="chem-val">7.40 &plusmn; 0.05</span> down to acidic <span class="chem-val">6.50</span> and <span class="chem-val">5.50</span> demonstrated that free hydronium ions (<span class="sci-tag">H<sub>3</sub>O<sup>+</sup></span>) neutralize carboxylates <span class="chem-val">Asp238</span>, <span class="chem-val">Glu239</span>, and <span class="chem-val">Asp350</span>, snapping salt bridges and opening lower transmembrane gates <span class="chem-val">Thr449 / Ser446</span>.
					</p>

					<!-- Physics & Chemistry Equation Block -->
					<div class="formula-box">
						<span class="formula-label">Biophysical Electrophysiology: Nernst &amp; Goldman Reversal Potential</span>
						<span class="formula-math">
							E<sub>rev</sub> = &minus;61.5 mV &bull; log<sub>10</sub> &times; [ (P<sub>Na</sub>[Na<sup>+</sup>]<sub>i</sub> + P<sub>K</sub>[K<sup>+</sup>]<sub>i</sub> + P<sub>Cl</sub>[Cl<sup>&minus;</sup>]<sub>o</sub>) &divide; (P<sub>Na</sub>[Na<sup>+</sup>]<sub>o</sub> + P<sub>K</sub>[K<sup>+</sup>]<sub>o</sub> + P<sub>Cl</sub>[Cl<sup>&minus;</sup>]<sub>i</sub>) ]
						</span>
						<span style="font-size: 0.82em; color: #64748b; margin-top: 0.3rem; display: block;">
							Depolarization shift: &Delta;V<sub>m</sub> = &minus;70 mV &rarr; &minus;45 mV at inward current density J<sub>Na</sub> = 14.8 &plusmn; 1.2 pA/pF.
						</span>
					</div>

					<p>
						In saliva, high-molecular-weight glycoproteins (<span class="sci-tag">MUC5B</span> and <span class="sci-tag">MUC7</span>) normally partner with bicarbonate ions (<span class="sci-tag">HCO<sub>3</sub><sup>&minus;</sup></span>) to buffer ambient oral acidity. When this buffer collapses, dental tubules leak dentinal fluid according to Hagen-Poiseuille hydrodynamics:
					</p>

					<!-- Fluid Dynamics Equation Block -->
					<div class="formula-box">
						<span class="formula-label">Hydrodynamic Fluid Shear Stress in Dentinal Microtubules</span>
						<span class="formula-math">
							Q = ( &pi; &bull; &Delta;P &bull; r<sup>4</sup> ) &divide; ( 8 &bull; &eta; &bull; L ) &nbsp;=&nbsp; 4.62 &times; 10<sup>&minus;9</sup> cm<sup>3</sup>/sec &bull; Pa
						</span>
					</div>

					<p>
						Unlike transient channels that inactivate within 100 to 300 ms, sensory nerves express <strong>ASIC3</strong> at 5&times; to 10&times; higher concentrations. Between pH 6.2 and 6.7, ASIC3 locks into an unbroken, non-inactivating window current, generating non-stop 10/10 neuropathic burning.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="font-notes">
					<strong>Why it works:</strong> Inter is the world gold-standard for technical interfaces and research papers. Tall x-height, neutral geometric discipline, and features explicit tabular numerals (numeral <strong>1</strong> has a crisp, sharp top spur that never collides with adjacent capital letters).
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- 3. COMBINATION 5: PUBLIC SANS -->
			<div class="variant-card var-public" id="card-var-public">
